  "verbalization": "Terbutaline, a bronchodilator, is linked to SNU-387 through a series of molecular interactions that involve the MIP (Methylenedioxyphenylironic acid) and other compounds. The evidence suggests that terbutaline acts as a target for multiple compounds, including 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One and (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol, both of which are targets of SNU-387. This indicates a potential mechanism where terbutaline indirectly influences SNU-387 through these intermediates. The presence of multiple pathways highlights a possible dependency on these compounds, suggesting that terbutaline may interact with SNU-387 via a complex network of molecular targets. The integration of these findings supports the idea that terbutaline's effects on SNU-387 are mediated through a series of biochemical interactions, emphasizing the importance of these intermediates in the overall mechanism.",
